LaBraM takes windows of any whole number of seconds up to 16 s, the length its pretrained time embeddings cover, instead of exactly 15 s: braindecode 2.0 loads the checkpoint at any window length. A longer window, whose extra time embeddings would be untrained, or one that does not divide into 1 s patches is refused. `FoundationModelSpec.pretrained_n_times`, `pretrained_window_seconds` and the `n_times` argument of `check_capability` are removed; no other model had a fixed window.
